// REJECTS: URL is not valid
//
// `clusterDetails: # URL { 'http://...' }#` with the url QUOTED. The island body is not Legend
// grammar at all: the text between the braces is handed to a URL island parser which runs it
// through java.net's URL machinery, so quotes are part of the string and make it malformed.
// The legal spelling is bare -- `# URL { http://dummyurl.com:1234/api }#` -- and it is the one
// place in this corpus where a url is NOT a quoted string.
//
// Two divergences in one construct. A rewrite that lexes island bodies as Legend tokens sees a
// STRING and accepts it happily; and a rewrite that treats the island as an opaque payload,
// deferring validation to compile time, accepts every malformed url. legend-engine parses AND
// validates the url before the element exists.
//
// Compare ../fixtures/t2-deephaven.pure, where `serverUrl:` in the neighbouring connection IS
// a quoted string and the unquoted form is refused with "Unexpected token 'http'" -- opposite
// conventions, adjacent grammars.
###Connection
Elasticsearch7ClusterConnection fixture::neg::QuotedClusterUrl
{
  store: fixture::neg::Store;
  clusterDetails: # URL { 'http://dummyurl.com:1234/api' }#;
  authentication: # UserPassword {
    username: 'u';
    password: EnvironmentSecret { envVariableName: 'v'; };
  }#;
}
